body:
Rebased and included methods.

I couldn't find a way to test from GDScript, so I've tested with the following `test_user_bench.cpp` to stress test each function individually from C++ (`GDScriptNativeClass::_get()` had to be made `public` for it):
```cpp
#include "tests/test_macros.h"

TEST_FORCE_LINK(test_user_bench)

#include <chrono>
#include <cstdio>
#include "modules/gdscript/gdscript.h"

static void user_bench() {
	const int N = 100'000'000;
	static Variant sink = 0;

	Ref<GDScriptNativeClass> nc = memnew(GDScriptNativeClass("Node2D"));

	auto t0 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
	for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
		nc->_get(SNAME("set_position"), sink);
	}
	auto t1 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();

	double ns_per_op = std::chrono::duration<double, std::nano>(t1 - t0).count() / N;
	printf("Benchmark result: %.1f ns/op (sink %zu)\n", ns_per_op, (size_t)sink);

	auto t2 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
	Callable::CallError e;
	for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
		nc->callp(SNAME("set_position"), nullptr, 0, e);
	}
	auto t3 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();

	double ns_per_op2 = std::chrono::duration<double, std::nano>(t3 - t2).count() / N;
	printf("Benchmark result: %.1f ns/op (sink %zu)\n", ns_per_op2, (size_t)sink);
}

REGISTER_TEST_COMMAND("user-bench", &user_bench)

```

Build command: `scons -j8 target=editor linker=mold dev_build=yes optimize=debug werror=yes tests=yes`

Results (`_get`):
|Run|ns/op before|ns/op after|
|-|-|-|
|1|47.8|13.9|
|2|46.0|14.0|
|3|45.8|13.9|

Results (`callp`):
|Run|ns/op before|ns/op after|
|-|-|-|
|1|28.4|10.4|
|2|25.6|10.4|
|3|25.6|10.4|

In average, getting a method through `_get()` becomes around **3.34x faster**, and through `callp()` becomes **2.55x faster**.
